{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The mother of Jacob and Esau.</b> It was necessary to write this, so that you not wonder: how did a wicked man like Esau emerge from two righteous people like Isaac and Rebekah? Therefore it says: 'the brother of Rebekah, the mother of Jacob and Esau,' to tell you, as they say in general, that most sons resemble the mother's brother — Esau resembled Laban, his mother's brother. Another interpretation: <b>the mother of Jacob and Esau</b> — for the benefit of both of them it was intended, as it is written: 'Why should I lose you both in one day.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:26.267711481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}